# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
.EuroVenv/
EuroferMicro_venv/
*.egg-info/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# C++ build artifacts
*/build/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.o
*.a

# Output (large result files — regenerate from notebooks).
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /: excluding the DIRECTORY makes git refuse
# to descend, and no negation below could then re-include anything inside it.
*/output/*

# EXEMPT: the designated reference run is tracked.  Everything else under
# output/ regenerates from a notebook; this one does not, in the sense that
# matters -- its figures and provenance.md are what published results are
# checked against, and two files read the directory BY NAME:
#     radcluster_code/digital_twin/verification/runs.py:33        (REFERENCE)
#     radcluster_code/digital_twin/verification/make_tables.py:72
# so the verification campaign cannot run on a fresh clone without it.  Left
# untracked it would exist on one disk, which is exactly how the original
# make_figures.py was lost.  32 files, 3.4 MB.
#
# This pins a timestamped directory name -- UPDATE IT when the reference run is
# superseded, and update those two files in the same commit.
!radcluster_code/output/20260906_063055_full_system_bin_moment_CD_fission_I80000V20000_im5vm5/
# ...but not its 37 MB plot_data.pkl: a regenerable cache, and a pickle of live
# InputData/RateEquations objects that will not load after a class refactor.  It
# is 92% of the directory and the worst possible archival format.
radcluster_code/output/*/plots/plot_data.pkl

# Temporary / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
~$*

# VSCode (keep settings.json, ignore local)
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json

# Campaign runtime state (pid of the detached worker; per-machine, never shared)
radcluster_code/digital_twin/results/*.pid

# Graceful-halt sentinel. LOCAL ONLY: it was committed in 8a600c7 and every
# machine that pulled it halted at startup, because run_ensemble checks
# STOP_FILE.exists() inside the submission loop. Never version this.
radcluster_code/digital_twin/CAMPAIGN_STOP

# Per-machine "already tallied" sentinels (zero-byte, written by ad-hoc
# tally loops, referenced by nothing that is versioned). Local like *.pid.
radcluster_code/digital_twin/results/*.seen

# Verification campaign (docs/Formulation/verification_campaign/paper_revision_verification_plan.md).
# .sync/ is a git WORKTREE for the campaign-verification branch: coordination
# runs there so a pull can never move a file underneath a running solver in the
# main checkout -- the dead-inode failure run_ensemble.py documents.  logs/ is
# per-machine live progress, rewritten per solver step; the campaign board on
# the branch is the shared record.
radcluster_code/digital_twin/verification/.sync/
radcluster_code/digital_twin/verification/logs/

# LaTeX build artifacts (the .tex and the .pdf are tracked; the rest regenerate)
docs/Formulation/**/*.aux
docs/Formulation/**/*.log
docs/Formulation/**/*.out
docs/Formulation/**/*.toc
docs/Formulation/**/*.fls
docs/Formulation/**/*.fdb_latexmk

# Doxygen code reference (docs/doxygen/Doxyfile): the HTML regenerates in a few
# seconds and is built by .github/workflows/documentation.yml.  The */build/
# rule above only reaches one directory level, so this one is listed by name.
docs/doxygen/build/

# Claude Code local working state — never shared.
# "Claude outputs/" is a scratch drop for generated drafts (the GCD rebuttal
# lived here); .claude/ holds per-machine session state: settings.json, the
# worktrees/ registry, and memory/.  The committed .claude/memory/ copy had
# already drifted out of step with the live harness memory it was supposed to
# mirror, so it was syncing a stale snapshot, not sharing anything.
Claude outputs/
.claude/

# Archived modules — kept on disk for reproducibility, not pushed.  276 MB of
# superseded code (RadCluster_1_0 alone is 140 MB) that nothing outside
# archive/ imports or reads; the only references anywhere were the two build/
# and output/ rules above, now redundant and removed.
#
# Untracking does NOT discard them.  Every file stays in the history: the last
# commit that carried the directory is e9f92c3, so
#     git checkout e9f92c3 -- archive/
# restores the whole tree, and tags v2.0.0 (RadCluster_2_0) and
# eurofer_cd-final (Eurofer_CD) pin the states CLAUDE.md cites.  What changes
# is that a FRESH CLONE no longer materialises archive/ in the working tree.
archive/

# The user's global ignore file (~/.gitignore_global) starts with ".*", which
# hides every dotfile -- including .github/.  A repo .gitignore outranks the
# global one, so this negation is what keeps CI workflows trackable without a
# "git add -f" every time.  Without it a new workflow is silently never staged.
!.github/
!.github/**
